---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { PAGES } from '../../lib/guides';
import { OPERATORS } from '../../lib/engine/repay';
const lang = 'en';
const n = PAGES.length + 1;
---
<PageLayout title="Radif Partners, publisher of UK Delay Repay: who we are" description="Who publishes UK Delay Repay, where every band, divisor and time limit comes from, what the calculators do with what you type, and what the site never sells." lang={lang} jsonLd={[organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><p class="kicker">About</p><h1 class="mt-0 text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Who is behind {SITE_NAMES[lang]}</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <div class="not-prose mb-6"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">{AUTHOR_NAME}</p><p class="text-navy-700">{AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p></div>
    <p>{SITE_NAMES[lang]} is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that builds free tools on public rules and public data. This site is for passengers in Great Britain whose train was late or cancelled and who want to know, in a minute, what they are owed, by when they must claim, and where.</p>
    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>It applies the published Delay Repay scheme of {OPERATORS.length} operators to the ticket, price and delay you enter, for singles, returns and season tickets, and gives the amount, the band, the next band and the last day to claim. It explains refunds after cancellations, strike days, missed connections, the Rail Ombudsman, railcards and split tickets, each with a calculator. It sends you to each operator's own claim form. Everything is free, needs no account, and what you type stays in your browser.</p>
    <h2>Where the rules come from</h2>
    <p>From primary sources only: each operator's Passenger's Charter or Delay Repay terms, the National Rail Conditions of Travel, the Rail Ombudsman, GOV.UK announcements of the Department for Transport, the Office of Rail and Road's statistics on delay compensation claims, the Consumer Rights Act 2015 and the Railcards website of the Rail Delivery Group. Every page links to the texts behind it. Where an operator's website could not be read directly, its terms were read on an archived copy, and the source says so. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> explains each calculation.</p>
    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>We are not a train company, National Rail, the Rail Delivery Group, the Rail Ombudsman, a ticket retailer or a claims company. We cannot see your booking, make a claim or receive a payment. The amounts are estimates from published schemes: the operator decides your claim. The site uses no official logo or brand.</p>
    <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
    <p>The site sells no service, takes no commission, collects no contact details and recommends no firm. If advertising is added one day, it will never sit inside a calculator, and it cannot use what you type, which never leaves your browser.</p>
    <h2>Tell us when something is wrong</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the page and the rule, ideally with a link to the operator's current terms. The <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> explains how a correction is made and dated. The site has {n} pages of guides and calculators.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600">Schemes and rules last checked on <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-GB')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
